    "done_when": "imas_ink.figures.time_trace_figure_mpl accepts each panel as one TimeSeries or a list of them; InkStyle gains trace_linestyle (default solid); _render_timeseries_mpl gains keyword arguments color (default None, the colour cycle as today) and label_axes (default True), and the panel loop draws a list's first series exactly as a single series is drawn today and each later series by calling _render_timeseries_mpl directly with color set to the first line's colour and label_axes=False, so a later series adds a line in its own style's trace_linestyle and sets no y-label, x-label or legend; render_mpl's signature is unchanged; _render_timeseries_alt applies trace_linestyle; the altair dash mapping used for wall_linestyle and trace_linestyle accepts matplotlib's shorthand forms ('-', '--', ':', '-.') as well as the named ones and both renderers draw the same style for each; tests/unit/test_vessel_units.py builds a figure whose one panel holds two TimeSeries and asserts both lines are on that axes, the second dashed and in the first line's colour, the y-label is the first series' and no legend was added, asserts a single-series panel still draws one line, and asserts the altair wall and trace renderers map '--' to a dash; 'uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/unit' adds no failure against the base revision, and 'uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ink tests' adds no finding against the base revision",
